<p>NOTE: 1997 nine-month results include a charge of $445,000 or $1.26/shr for a Savings Association Insurance Fund assessment and a one-time $131,000 (after tax) or $0.37/shr recovery of a prior period loss on the sale of real estate owned properties. Without the special assessment and prior-period loss recovery, net income for the 1997 nine months would have been $439,000 or $1.24/shr.</p>
